Add the device tree for the ASUS Vivobook S 16 S3607QA, a 16" laptop
based on the Snapdragon X X1-26-100 (X1P42100, Purwa): BOE eDP panel
with PMIC PWM backlight, Adreno X1-45, WCN6855 NFA765 Wi-Fi/BT,
2x WSA8845 speakers and a WCD9385 headset codec, NVMe, USB-A, USB-C
and HDMI.

It was derived from the Windows ACPI tables of the device and the
Vivobook S15 device tree.

The CPU thermal zones get 90 C passive trips with cpufreq cooling: the
SoC dtsi only has critical trips, and without an EC fan driver the
machine reached its thermal limit under sustained load.

Developed with the help of an AI coding assistant (Anthropic Claude),
which drafted the changes from the Windows ACPI tables, existing device
trees and test logs; reviewed, built and tested on the device by the
submitter.

